<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<language>
















	
	<entry name="Orks/Vehicles" value="Kult ov Speed"/>
	<entry name="Orks/VehiclesDescription" value="This building produces Basic Vehicles as well as generates resources. Units produced here typically cost ore."/>

	<entry name="Orks/Infantry" value="Pile O' Dakka"/>
	<entry name="Orks/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Basic infantry and Heroes as well as generates resources. Units produced here typically cost food and ore."/>

	<entry name="Orks/Colonizers" value="Mek Bitz Yard"/>
	<entry name="Orks/ColonizersDescription" value="Building that produces Meks, Killa Kans, Mek Gunz and Deffkoptas as well as generates resources. Units produced here typically cost energy and ore/food."/>

	<entry name="Orks/Construction" value="Scrap Shedz"/>
	<entry name="Orks/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Orks/ConstructionFlavor" value="Ork buildings are inelegant constructions of waste materials and any scrap that the Meks don't need. The Grotz aren't known to be good architects, but the Orks don't care so long as they get a good fight."/>

	<entry name="Orks/AdvancedVehicles" value="Da Dread Forge"/>
	<entry name="Orks/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Deff Dreads, Kill Burstas, Big Meks, Burna-Bommers, Gorkanauts and Wazbom Blastajets. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore, Food and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Orks/AdvancedInfantry" value="Da Boss Pit"/>
	<entry name="Orks/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Aircraft Units like: Warbosses, Flash Gitz, Meganobz, Squighog Boyz, Dakkajets and Gargantuan Squiggoth. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food and Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Orks/Housing" value="Da Mob Pen"/>
	<entry name="Orks/HousingDescription" value="Special Ork building that increases the population limit and can also produce Ork Boyz. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 0 population to operate."/>
	<entry name="Orks/HousingFlavor" value="Where boyz gather, fight, and get ready for a proper scrap."/>

	<entry name="Orks/Heroes" value="Da Boss Pit"/>
	<entry name="Orks/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Aircraft Units like: Warbosses, Flash Gitz, Meganobz, Squighog Boyz, Dakkajets and Gargantuan Squiggoth. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food and Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>
	<entry name="Orks/HeroesFlavor" value="Only da strongest Orks come outta Da Boss Pit. Everyone else gets stomped, squished, or turned into a lesson fer da next fight." />



	<entry name="Tyranids/Aircraft" value="Capillary Tower"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces flying monstrous creatures, Tervigon and Hive Tyrant as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/AircraftFlavor" value="Tall as a human Hive City, Capillary Towers are the backbone of Tyranid conquest. Here, the resources of the planet are siphoned from Reclamation Pools and fed up through the troposphere to meet the umbilical tongues of orbiting Hive ships. On Gladius, the Towers have no Hive Ships to feed. Instead, Gargoyles and Hive Crones crawl from birthing sacs on the Tower's sides and wait for their newborn wings to stiffen so they can join the war."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/Thropes" value="Aedanthropum"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/ThropesDescription" value="Building that produces Thropes like Malanthrope, Venomthropes and Zoahnthropes as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/ThropesFlavor" value="Not all Tyranid creatures are equal; whilst Termagants and Hormagaunts require little focus and unspecialised resources, the construction and gestation of more complex creatures can take more care. In isolated hives like that of Gladius, the diverse support creatures the Imperium calls Anthropia—Venomthropes, Zoanthropes and Malanthropes—all emerge from a specialised biostructure of gristly columns, podia and caverns."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/Vehicles" value="Brood Nexus"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces infantry and beasts with a ranged focus like Termagants, Tyranid Warriors, Hive Guards and Tervigons as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/VehiclesFlavor" value="Within the Brood Nexus, biomass is reshaped and reborn. Endless waves of creatures are gestated under the guiding will of the Hive Mind, each organism perfectly adapted for the swarm’s advance."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/Heroes" value="Stalker Nest"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces infantry and beast that are more independant from the Hive Mind like Gargoyles, Tyrannocytes, Genestealers and Lictors as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/HeroesFlavor" value="The Stalker Nest breeds terror unseen. From its shadowed chambers emerge infiltrators and airborne horrors, striking without warning and dismantling the enemy from within."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/Infantry" value="Predator Lair"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry and beasts with a melee focus like Hormagaunts, Tyranid Warriors, Tyranid Prime and Raveners as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/InfantryFlavor" value="The Predator Lair pulses with feral intent. Here, the Hive Mind forges its most aggressive hunters, unleashing relentless bioforms driven by instinct, speed, and an insatiable urge to kill."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/Construction" value="Megafauna Sac"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/ConstructionFlavor" value="Nothing reflects the inhumanity of a hive more than the Megafauna Sac. To a human eye, its smooth membranous dome is reminiscent of a design for a museum. However, when it tears itself asunder to reveal another giant biostructure, pulsating and screaming in its birth throes—when that building is half-dragged, half-crawls its towering flesh into position—when the Sac gums itself back together and ripper swarms consume its afterbirth—the human mind then sees it as truly alien."/>




	<entry name="Tyranids/AdvancedInfantry" value="Maleceptorium"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Monsters like: Hive-Tyrant, Biovore, Haruspex, Maleceptor and Tyrannofex. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/AdvancedVehicles" value="Behemoth Gestation Pit"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Monsters like: Hive-Tyrant, Carnifex, Exocrine, Hivecrone, Trygon and Harpy. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>


	<entry name="Tyranids/LateGameUnits" value="Leviathan Bio-Forge"/>
	<entry name="Tyranids/LateGameUnitsDescription" value="Building that produces late-game Monsters like: Trygon, Tyrannofex, Norn Emissary and Scythed Hierodule <br/><br/>Requires 3 build slots and 3 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>



	<entry name="Eldar/Heroes" value="Wayfarer Enclave"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Rangers, Spiritseer, Heavy Weapon Platforms and Wraithblades as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Energy and Ore/Food as part of their cost."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/Infantry" value="Asuryan's Crucible"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces basic infantry like: Guardians, Autarchs, Howling Banshees, Dark Reapers, Fire Dragons and Warp Spiders, as well as generates resources.  <br/><br/>Units trained here require Food and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Eldar/InfantryFlavor" value="Asuryan, the Phoenix King, was the chief of the Aeldari Gods and the last to be consumed by Slaanesh during the fall of the Aeldari. He has long been an inspiration to the Craftworld Aeldari, who often refer to themselves as ‘Asuryani’. At this muster ground, new arrivals to Gladius are equipped and assigned to squads before being tested in the field."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/Construction" value="Bonesingers Chantry"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Eldar/ConstructionFlavor" value="Many of the paths that Aeldari walk in their long lives are non-violent—indeed, most are, for the Craftworld Aeldari were those who rejected the hedonistic lives of their peers for one of contemplation. Bonesingers are artisans who psychically manipulate Wraithbone into the structures and machinery that Aeldari use."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/Vehicles" value="Greater Ingress"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces skimmers and jetbikes like: Shining Spears, Farseer Skyrunner, Hornet and Vypers as well as generates resources.  <br/><br/>Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Eldar/VehiclesFlavor" value="This extension to the Webway Portal allows larger vehicles to access Gladius Prime. Without it, the Aeldari forces would just be infantry and jetbikes—enough for a Harlequin Troupe or a Biel-Tan vanguard perhaps, but not for a true war effort."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/Aircraft" value="Portal Spire"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft as well as generates resources.Units trained here require Energy and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Eldar/AircraftFlavor" value="Raised high above the ground, this coiled Webway opening enables Aeldari aircraft to travel straight from the immaterium to Gladius Prime whilst having a slower transition of air pressure, composition and local gravity compared to the unearthly forms present in the twisted space between the stars."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/AdvancedVehicles" value="Prism Foundry"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Wave Serpent, Fire Prism, Crimson Hunter, War Walkers and Scorpions. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/AdvancedInfantry" value="Spirit Forge"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Vehicles Units like: Wraithlords, Avatar of Khaine, Warlocks, Wraithknight, Hemlock Wraithfighter and Scorpion. <br/><br/>Units here cost Energy and Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Eldar/Headquarters1" value="Webway Redoubt"/>
	<entry name="Eldar/Headquarters1Description" value="Headquarters building that generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Eldar/Headquarters1Flavor" value="The Webway riddles Gladius Prime, but many of the gateways have been lost. Even those that survive are unimaginably ancient, but still they stand, ignored by the younger races. Around them, the Aeldari build emplacements and machinery, to stabilise the gateways renewed connection with the immaterium and defend it against incursion."/>



	<entry name="Drukhari/Infantry" value="Kabalite Stronghold"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Food and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/InfantryFlavor" value="The Kabals of the Drukhari are a mix of criminal cartel, pirate fraternity and noble household, like the ancient Earth Mafia or Triads. A Kabal takes only the best (or worst) of Drukhari society—sadists, thieves, murderers—in other words, the pillars of the Drukhari community. They also supply the military strength of Commorragh, deployed in its defense or on real-space raids."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/Vehicles" value="Dark Foundry"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Skimmers and Jetbikes as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/VehiclesFlavor" value="The material foundries of Commorragh exist deep beneath the city, where countless Drukhari and xenos workers live and die without ever seeing the light of its black suns, kept in constant pain, torment and misery, driven on by a fear of death. The Kabal requisitioners do their best to replicate this ideal wherever they travel."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/Heroes" value="Fleshcraft Coven"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Wyches, Wracks, Haemonculi and Chronos as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/HeroesFlavor" value="Within the Fleshcraft Covens, pain is currency and flesh is clay. Haemonculi labor endlessly, flensing, stitching and reshaping broken bodies into instruments of agony and war."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/Construction" value="Taskmaster Estate"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/ConstructionFlavor" value="“So great was the fear, so horrible the punishments, that the threat of pain was a much greater motivation than the pain itself, so we seldom had to use it. But use it we did, an unpredictable torture driven by our insidious depravity and our labourers responded with alacrity…” — Ilthea the Faded, former Archon of the Withered Heart Kabal, prisoner of Inquisitor Jey Carnaa."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/Aircraft" value="Aerie"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Ore and Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/AircraftFlavor" value="The ancient spires of Commorragh are host inside and out to horrors. Atop them are the homes of Scourges and Hellions, Drukhari who ride the air currents wafting up from the impossible city’s impossible depths, from the machinery and torment and death. Even here, on the doomed world of Gladius Prime, these aethereal monsters have their place."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/AdvancedVehicles" value="Void Barge Docks"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Ravager, Talos, Voidraven Bomber and Tantalus. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/AdvancedInfantry" value="Obsidian Bladeshrine"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Aircraft Units like: Helions, Archons, Trueborn, Incubi and Razorwing Jetfighter. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food, Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Drukhari/Influence" value="The Enslavement Spire"/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/InfluenceDescription" value="Special Drukhari Building, that generates influence and increases the population limit. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 1 population to operate."/>
	<entry name="Drukhari/InfluenceFlavor" value="Rising above the shadowed districts, the Enslavement Spire is both habitation and prison. Within its barbed halls, captives are broken, catalogued and displayed, their suffering fueling the authority of the Archons. Every scream reinforces Drukhari dominance, and every chained soul is another measure of power."/>






	
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Cult" value="Cult of Chaos"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/CultDescription" value="Building that produces Cultist Units and Deamons as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Food as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/CultFlavor" value="What are gods without followers? Here, Cultists and Dark Apostles alike plot to bring converts to the worship of Chaos—not a hard task on Gladius, once people see the inhuman Xenos, the undoubted effects of the Dark Gods’ powers, and the Daemonic shapes lingering in the chancel."/>


	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Heroes" value="Cult of Chaos"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Cultist Units and Deamons as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Food as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/HeroesFlavor" value="What are gods without followers? Here, Cultists and Dark Apostles alike plot to bring converts to the worship of Chaos—not a hard task on Gladius, once people see the inhuman Xenos, the undoubted effects of the Dark Gods’ powers, and the Daemonic shapes lingering in the chancel."/>


	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Infantry" value="Abominator's Genelab"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry like: Chaos Space Marines, Chaos Lords, Khorne Berzerkers, Havocs, Plague Marines and Noise Marines, as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Food and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/InfantryFlavor" value="Not all Chaos Space Marines date from the 30th millenium—others are recruited from civilians, brutally altered with geneseed taken from a fallen Marine. At this genelab, fallen Apothecaries operate on the strongest cultists drawn from Gladius’ ruined Hives. The few who survive the Abominators’ operations are implanted with Progenoid glands and recruited as new Chaos Space Marines."/>

	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Aircraft" value="Helhaunted Eyrie"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces Lategame Units like heldrakes, Obliterators and Brass Scorpions as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AircraftFlavor" value="10,000 years ago the Heldrakes were fighter craft, piloted by the cream of the Adeptus Astartes. Now, they are hideous amalgams of man and machine, formed by millennia of war into dragon-like creatures that live to fight. This artificial eyrie allows the Warpsmiths and Master of Possession to monitor the Heldrakes and even attempt to replicate their age-old creation."/>

	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Vehicles" value="Infernal Fabricator"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Basic ground vehicles like Rhinos, Venomcrawlers, Helbrute and Warpsmiths as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/VehiclesFlavor" value="Normally confined to the Soul Forges of the Warp, these incomprehensible mechanoid structures are responsible for the creation of all Daemon vehicles. Here, Mechatendril-wreathed Warpsmiths oversee the breaking and corruption of Machine Spirits of captured Imperial vehicles, as well as the forcible incorporation of Lesser Daemons, machinery and tortured flesh into Daemon Engines."/>


	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AdvancedVehicles" value="Dark Forge"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces  Mid and late-game Vehicles and Warmachines like: Maulerfiends, Forgefiends, Defiler, Land Raiders and Greater Brass Scropions. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AdvancedInfantry" value="Hall of the Everchosen"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Aircraft Units like: Rubric Marines, Daemon Prince, Warp Talons, Chaos Terminators, Obliterators and Helldrakes. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food, Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/Loyalty" value="Meadow of Sorrow"/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/LoyaltyDescription" value="Special Chaos Building, that increase loyalty and can also produce Chaos Cultist. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 1 population to operate."/>
	<entry name="ChaosSpaceMarines/LoyaltyFlavor" value="It can’t have been a follower of Khorne who named this plain a ‘meadow’—allegory isn’t a concomitant of the Blood God’s troops. Whoever coined it, the metaphor is apt—the carefully-planted rows, tended conscientiously, the gaps refilled as they empty. But the Slaaneshi garden these fields, constantly devising unholy pleasures for their God’s honour at the expense of its victims."/>






	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/Auxiliaries" value="Ecclesiarchal Reinforcements"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AuxiliariesDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft and imperial knights as well as generates resources. Units here cost Requisitions and Energy."/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AuxiliariesFlavor" value="Unusually for an Adepta Sororitas mission, not all the troops here are Battle Sisters. Though the other local forces of the Imperium have proved to be untrustworthy, the remaining Imperial Navy and Knightly Houses have found themselves with divided loyalties. Those who have sided with the Adepta Sororitas have been assigned these unprepossessing buildings for accommodation, repair and habitation."/>
	
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/Construction" value="Ministorum Workshop"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/ConstructionFlavor" value="More primitive it might be than the great manufactora of the Adeptus Mechanicus and Adeptus Administratum, but what the workers of a Ministorum workshop lack in technical knowledge, they make up for in religious fervour and craftsmanship. The buildings they create are not merely functional—they are works of worship and art for the God-Emperor himself."/>
	
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/Heroes" value="Legatines' Priory"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces heroes and Hospitallers as well as generates resources. Units here cost Requisitions and Energy."/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/HeroesFlavor" value="The highest-ranking Sisters of an Order are a mix of warriors, healers and spiritual leaders—but not all of them have formal positions, despite the fervour and veneration they inspire in their peers. This priory serves a gathering point for these Legatines when away from their orders, with all the comforts of home—shrines, chapels, cells and places of ritual scourging."/>

	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/Infantry" value="Battle Chapel"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry like: Battle Sisters, Arco-Flagellants, Dominions, Retributors, Sisters Repentia and Celestian Insidiants, as well as generates resources. Units here cost Requisitions."/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/InfantryFlavor" value="The final stage of a novice’s career occurs in the Battle Chapel. Here, the cantus is trained in the use of her sacred weaponry—bolter, flamer, melta—and confirmed in her faith, proof against heresy. Normally, once trained, she would visit a primary Convent’s great hall for assignment to an Order—but on Gladius Prime, where no escape is possible, she enters straight into the ranks of her sistren, defending this world."/>

	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/Vehicles" value="Anointed Hangar"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Seraphim, Immolators and Mortifier as well as generates resources. Units here cost Requisitions."/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/VehiclesFlavor" value="The vehicles of the Adepta Sororitas are ancient—relic battle tanks of long-ago crusades. In this hangar, Exorcists, Castigators and Immolators have their machine spirits revived by the Ministorum technicians, are sprinkled with sacred oils, and sacred incantations handed down for thousands of years. To the T’au and Votann, this would be rank superstition—yet the machines work with a deadly efficiency."/>

	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AdvancedVehicles" value="Armory of the Faithful"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Castigator, Exorcist, Avenger Strike Fighter and Cerastus Knight-Lancer. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AdvancedInfantry" value="Sanctum of the Martyred Saint"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Warmaschines like: Zephyrim, Saint Celestine, Lighning Fighter, Celestian Sacresants, Paragon Warsuits. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/HolySite" value="Crown Basilica of the Emperor"/>
	<entry name="SistersOfBattle/HolySiteDescription" value="Unique Sororitas Building, that produces Requisitions, Research and Influence. Doubles its resource production if built on a Holy Site. <br/><br/>Clearing tiles on a Holy Site is prohibited, as doing so will cause the site to disappear. The Emperor demands that his holy ground remain untouched."/>






	<entry name="Tau/Heroes" value="Auxiliary Deployment Hub"/>
	<entry name="Tau/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Kroots, Vespids, Etherals and Commanders as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Food as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Tau/HeroesFlavor" value="Commanders like ShadowSun and PureTide are rare individuals, raised up by the Ethereals to be representatives of all that is good and true about the T’au. So few are they that, when not deployed on campaigns, they are placed in stasis until the next time they are needed."/>

	<entry name="Tau/Aircraft" value="Kor'vattra Nacelle"/>
	<entry name="Tau/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Tau/AircraftFlavor" value="The Air Caste’s slender limbs and hollow bones are so ill-suited to life on the ground that they are often called ‘The Invisible Caste’ by planet-dwellers. Their nacelles are combined factories, hangars and living spaces—throughout holding technology that reduces the effects of Gladius Prime’s gravity on their delicate physiology."/>
	
	<entry name="Tau/Construction" value="Brachyuran'm Foundry"/>
	<entry name="Tau/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tau/ConstructionFlavor" value="The Brachyuran might not be suited to combat—after all, they mostly closely resemble crustaceans similar to tiny Terran crabs—but their compact form conceals a fierce technical intelligence, ideally suited to delicate construction. In this foundry, teams of Brachyuran can aid the Earth Caste in building structures, from the macro to the micro level."/>

	<entry name="Tau/Infantry" value="Shas'm Barracks"/>
	<entry name="Tau/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry, Battlesuits, Fireblades and Commanders as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Food and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Tau/InfantryFlavor" value="In this smooth-skinned blister-bunker, Fireblades and other T’au veterans train up the members of the fire caste from Shas’saal recruits into full-blown Shas’la Fire Warriors, administering the Trial of Fire at the end of their fourth year."/>

	<entry name="Tau/Vehicles" value="Fio'xar Arsenal"/>
	<entry name="Tau/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces ground vehicles as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Ore and Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Tau/VehiclesFlavor" value="Here the dour Earth caste craft the unique skimmer vehicles available to the T’au military. Over time, they assure you, they will be able to increase their capabilities."/>

	<entry name="Tau/MonstrousCreatures" value="Xar'vesa Crisis Centre"/>
	<entry name="Tau/MonstrousCreaturesDescription" value="Building that produces big Battlesuits as well as generates research and influence. Units trained here require Ore and Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Tau/MonstrousCreaturesFlavor" value="Once a Fire Warrior has passed their Trial-By-Fire and proven themself, they are allowed to don the Her'ex'evre or Mantle of Heroes and pilot a battlesuit. Here, the iconic T’au machines are assembled by the Earth Caste, with Brachyuran technicians working on the fine internal mechanisms."/>

	<entry name="Tau/AdvancedVehicles" value="Kor'vattra Support Complex"/>
	<entry name="Tau/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Commanders, XV95 Ghostkeel Battlesuits, TX7 Hammerhead Gunship, AX3 Razorshark Strike Fighter, XV107 R'Varna Battlesuit and Tiger Shark. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Tau/AdvancedInfantry" value="Xar'vesa Crisis Centre"/>
	<entry name="Tau/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Vehicles Units like: Commanders, XV8 Crisis Battlesuits, XV88 BroadSide Battlesuits, XV104 Riptide Battlesuits, AX39 Sun Shark Bomber and KV128 Stormsurge. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food, Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Tau/Headquarters1" value="Tau'shiro HQ"/>
	<entry name="Tau/Headquarters1Description" value="Headquarters building that generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Tau/Headquarters1Flavor" value="Named after the Air Caste’s continent-sized space stations, this fortress acts as the central point of the colony-city. It is theoretically the solitary preserve of the Commanders in a military situation, but in practice is the seat of the colony’s Ethereals."/>





	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Aircraft" value="Voidport"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Ore and Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AircraftFlavor" value="This landing field was designed for larger craft—almost up to the intra-system scale—but with the endless warpstorms, it's been repurposed to house the Imperial air forces. Much like a Skyshield landing pad, it has limited field generators to protect grounded aircraft from incoming fire."/>
	
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Construction" value="Labour Corps"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/ConstructionFlavor" value="Whilst the Administratum runs the entire Empire of Man, the Departmento Munitorum is tasked solely with supplying the manpower and supplies for the Astra Militarum. Among their many tasks is the construction of large facilities, such as airfields or orbital stations. The poor grunts who have to do the work are the Labour Corps, indentured or penal workers and mind-wiped servitors."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Infantry" value="Imperial Barracks"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces basic infantry, Primaris Psyker and Tech-Priest Enginseers as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Food and Ore/Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/InfantryFlavor" value="Whilst the training of recruits to the Imperial Guard has none of the harrowing horrors suffered by Astartes initiates, the Munitorum still has to drill the strictures of the Empire into the tithed men and women that make up most Guard regiments. Here, at the Barracks, a planet's unpromising conscripts are turned into the true Astra Militarum—by giving them uniforms, guns and perhaps even some training."/>
	
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Vehicles" value="Manufactorum"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces basic ground vehicles like: Scout Sentinels, Chimeras, Hydras, Devil Dogs and Armoured Sentinels, as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/VehiclesFlavor" value="To call an Imperial Manufactorum a 'factory' is akin to calling a Catachan Devil an insect. These cyclopean structures are huge, forbidding temples to the Machine God, wherein his miracles—here vehicles of war—are created. Inside them, lowly menials are doomed to never see the planet's surface, as they ceaselessly minister to the blessed engines of Mars."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Heroes" value="Veteran Barracks"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid-game Infantry Units like: Lord Commissar, Tempestus Scions, Wyrdvane Psykers, Anti-Tank Guns and Attilan Rough Riders as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Food and Ore/Energy as part of their cost. Offers slightly higher production."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/HeroesFlavor" value="Sanctified by duty and blood, these barracks train proven warriors of the Astra Militarum. Each soldier who departs does so in the Emperor’s name, ready to pay the price of war once more."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedVehicles" value="Heavy Armour Complex"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Tank Commander, Leman Russ Tank, Deathstrike, Thunderbolt, Marauder Bomber and Baneblade. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedInfantry" value="Veteran Barracks"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid-game Infantry Units like: Lord Commissar, Tempestus Scions, Wyrdvane Psykers, Anti-Tank Guns and Attilan Rough Riders as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units trained here require Food and Ore/Energy as part of their cost. Offers slightly higher production."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedVehicles2" value="Heavy Support Foundry"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/AdvancedVehicles2Description" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Units like: Tank Commander, Basilisk, Bullgryns, Valkyrie, Rogal Dorn Tank and Baneblade. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore, Energy or Food. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Headquarters1" value="Basilica Administratum"/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Headquarters1Description" value="Headquarters building that generates resources."/>
	<entry name="AstraMilitarum/Headquarters1Flavor" value="The central administrative building of any Imperial colony, the magnificent Basilica is a temple to bureaucracy. Generations of plain-clad clerks live and die amidst tottering tomes, deciding the fate of star systems with the feeble thump of their stamps. As the saying goes, the Inquisition may burn you, the Astartes smite you—but only the Adeptus Administratum can torment you for your entire life."/>






	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Heroes" value="Sub-Cloister"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/HeroesDescription" value="Building that produces Cybernetica Datasmith, Tech-Priest Heroes, Electropriest and Kastellan Robots as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Food/Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/HeroesFlavor" value="A Sub-Cloister serves as a shelter and school for new Tech-Priests. Here, promising acolytes from the planet’s hive cities are trained in the many secrets of the Cult Mechanicus. Over time, if they survive, they find their calling, emerging as lowly Enginseers, fanatical Electro-Priests, cybernetic Data-Smiths or any of a myriad other non-combat specialisations."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Infantry" value="Genetor Caropraedium"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Food and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/InfantryFlavor" value="To say that the Astra Militarum training academies ‘produce’ soldiers would offend any Tech-Priest’s logic centres. Even the lowliest acolyte knows that humans are just one raw material in the production of effective soldiers, with circuits, bio-plastic and metal comprising a larger proportion of most Skitarii. After all, “flesh is fallible”!"/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Vehicles" value="Manufactorum Cybernetica"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/VehiclesDescription" value="Produces ground vehicles like: Ironstrider Ballistarii, Sydonian Dragoons, Skorpius Duneriders, Cinderfangs and Onager Dunecrawlers. Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/VehiclesFlavor" value="A Tech-Priest manufactorum is leagues ahead of its standard Imperial equivalent. Not technologically, of course—the Cult Mechanicus considers it more important to safeguard the technology they have and improving it is a Xenarite heresy that only Cawl himself might consider. Instead this building has superior rituals, unguents, chants, libations and so forth."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Aircraft" value="Basilikon Archaeoptera"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft and orders the infamous Imperial Knights as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Energy and Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AircraftFlavor" value="An Archaeoptera is just yet another Adeptus Mechanicus construction facility, albeit for flying machines rather than terrestrial. It has all the usual elements—the massed slave labour to build the machines, the medical facilities for all the amputations the pilots need to fit in, and the shrines to conduct the proper rituals over the Transvectors and Stratoraptors. In other words, a totally normal Tech-Priest manufactorum."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Construction" value="Artisan Constructorum"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/ConstructionFlavor" value="The simple title of ‘artisan’ conceals the immensity of what these Tech-Priests achieve. Not personally, of course, but through vast labour forces of mind-wiped servitors. Here, in the Constructorum, this army of once-men build the buildings and tools to enable the Tech-Priest’s efforts elsewhere."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Advanced" value="Macro-Manufactorum"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AdvancedDescription" value="Building that produces late-game infantry, tanks, and aircraft. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AdvancedVehicles" value="Macro-Manufactorum"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces late-game Vehicles and Aircraft like: Kastellan Robots, Archaeopter Transvector, Armiger Helverin, Archaeopter Stratoraptor and KnightCrusader. <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AdvancedInfantry" value="Legio Cybernetica Nexus"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Vehicles Units like: Kataphron Breacher, Sicarian Ruststalker, Kataphron Destroyer and Skorpius Disintegrator. <br/><br/>Units here cost Food and Ore. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Monastery" value="Monastery of the Omnissiah’s Lightning"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/MonasteryDescription" value="Building that produces a lot of Energy and can also produce Electropriests. <br/><br/> Requires 3 build slots and 3 population to operate."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/MonasteryFlavor" value="Within these sanctified halls, flesh is rendered unto the Omnissiah and repaid in lightning. Each prayer is a circuit, each scar a sacrament, and through suffering the Sacred Current flows eternal."/>

	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Headquarters1" value="Forge Temple"/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Headquarters1Description" value="Headquarters building that generates resources."/>
	<entry name="AdeptusMechanicus/Headquarters1Flavor" value="The Forge Temple is the centre of the Adeptus Mechanicus’ presence on a world. Is it a citadel of information, a repository of the remnants of humanity’s long-cherished knowledge… or the headquarters of a fanatical cult dedicated to hoarding information that could save humanity? To even think the latter would, of course, be heresy…"/>








	<entry name="SpaceMarines/Heroes" value="Reclusiam"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/HeroesDescription" value="Building that Produces Heroes, Tactical Marines, Apothecaries, and Techmarines with Thunderfire Cannons as well as generates resources.  <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions and Energy."/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/HeroesFlavor" value="For those rare ceremonies that require the attendance of every Battle Brother, the vastness of the Reclusiam allows the entire Chapter to gather. This is the most precious place in a fortress-monastery—home to its most sacred relics and, in a rare few, the very body of its Primarch. It is also the seat of the chapter's commanders and heroes."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/Aircraft" value="Assault Pads"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces Landspeeders, Assault Marines, Dreadnoughts, Storm Speeders and Primaris Inceptors as well as generates resources. <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions and Energy."/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AircraftFlavor" value="Staging area for the Chapter's aerial assault craft and transports, from whence battle-brothers may embark upon their endless crusade. The fortress-monastery's active gunships, interceptors, landing craft and even its mighty Thunderhawks are housed in a hive of hangars below the launch pads."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/Vehicles" value="Armoury"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/VehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces basic ground vehicles as well as generates resources.  <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions."/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/VehiclesFlavor" value="Home to anything that a Marine might employ to purge the battlefield of xenos and heretics, from the simplest combat knife to the most redoubtable of relics. The Master of Ordnance keeps a close watch upon the Chapter's wargear—only his gene-print can grant access to this titanic underground repository of weapons and vehicles."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/Infantry" value="Apothecarion"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/InfantryDescription" value="Building that produces infantry as well as generates resources. <br/><br/> Units here cost Requisitions."/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/InfantryFlavor" value="The Apothecarion provides medical support for wounded Battle-Brothers, and plays a vital role in the elevation of an Aspirant to a Space Marine. Both these functions pale into insignificance against the Apothecarion's other purpose—the preservation of its Chapter's unique gene-seed, from which new Space Marines are created. If the gene-seed is lost, so too is the Chapter."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/Construction" value="Orbital Relay"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/ConstructionFlavor" value="In normal times, the various Teleportaria would be used to transport troops to and from nearby starships. In these warptorn times, the Orbital Relay serves a more important function, communicating with the low-orbiting Battle Barge and calling down important requisitions for rapid surface deployment."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AdvancedVehicles" value="Forge Sanctum"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces late-game Vehicles and Walkers like: Predators, Redemptor Dreadnoughts, Primaris Repulsor Executioners and Land Raiders. <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AdvancedInfantry" value="Reliquary"/>
	<entry name="SpaceMarines/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces late-game Infantry and Aircraft Units like: Terminators, Stormtalon Gunships, Assault Terminators, Devastator Centurions, Stormraven Gunships and Thunderhawk Gunships. <br/><br/>Units here cost Requisitions and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>



	<entry name="Necrons/Heroes" value="Canoptek Matrix"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/HeroesDescription" value="Produces Canoptek Scarabs, Reanimators and Spyders, as well as the Cryptek hero(no research needed). Generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/HeroesFlavor" value="The tomb of the Phaeron, Overlord or Lord and his court, this is where all the most loyal and important retainers retreated to sleep away the centuries until the universe was ready again. Even now, great heroes still lie sleeping in its core, awaiting their Lords' call."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/Infantry" value="Summoning Core"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/InfantryDescription" value="Produces infantry like: Warriors, Flayed Ones, Deathmarks, Heavy Destroyers and Triarch Praetorians, as well as the Lord hero. Units trained here require Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/InfantryFlavor" value="Awakening the long-deactivated troops of a Necron dynasty is slow work, as is repairing those who fall in the field. The Canopteks and Crypteks of the Summoning Core diligently save those who recall to the city—and dismantle the rest for their rare Necrodermis."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/Vehicles" value="Hypostyle Temple"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/VehiclesDescription" value="Produces ground vehicles like: Tomb Blades, Ghost Arks, Annihilation Barges and Triarch Stalkers, as well as the Destroyer Lord hero. Units trained here require Ore as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/VehiclesFlavor" value="This high-roofed building is lined with pillars inside. Between them rest or float the great war machines of the Necrons. Deactivated Doomsday Arks, Annihilation Barges, Monoliths and Obelisks wait in serried ranks for the day when a Lord calls for their repair and they can lead his armies once more."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/Construction" value="Slave Mastaba"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/ConstructionDescription" value="Building that constructs new buildings as well as generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/ConstructionFlavor" value="Everyone has a place in Necron society. The weak-fleshed races of the Old Ones live out their days under crude shelters, where they scrape together their own food, before being sent out to excavate the Necron's long-buried tombs and retrieve the sleeping Necrons."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/Aircraft" value="Nameless Causeway"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/AircraftDescription" value="Building that produces aircraft, Obilisk and Tesseract Vault as well as generates resources. Units trained here require Ore and Energy as part of their cost."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/AircraftFlavor" value="If the Necron are dreaded across the known universe, their aircraft are doubly feared. The Doom Scythe and Night Scythe are fast, hardy and deadly to armoured opponents. Launching from a bleak expanse of stone, they devastate enemies with their irresistible assaults."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/EnergyOre" value="Extraction Matrix"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/EnergyOreDescription" value="Building that produces Ore and Energy aswell a small population limit increase. <br/><br/>Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>
	
	<entry name="Necrons/AdvancedVehicles" value="Hyperphase Nexus"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/AdvancedVehiclesDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Vehicles and Monsters like: Hexmark Destroyer, Canoptek Wraiths, Doomsday Ark, Doom Scythe, Obilisk and Seraptek Heavy Construct <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/AdvancedInfantry" value="Immortal Necropolis"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/AdvancedInfantryDescription" value="Building that produces Mid and late-game Infantry and Vehicles Units like: Immortals, Transcendent C´Tan, Night Scythe, Skorpekh Destoryers and Monoliths. <br/><br/>Units here cost Ore and Energy. Requires 2 build slots and 2 population to operate, but offers higher production."/>

	<entry name="Necrons/Headquarters1" value="Royal Court"/>
	<entry name="Necrons/Headquarters1Description" value="Headquarters building that generates resources."/>
	<entry name="Necrons/Headquarters1Flavor" value="The seat of the Necron Phaeron and his court is a great bleak building, one of the few great Necron buildings not originally built to venerate the dead. Instead, its shielding walls are a symbolic reflection of the intense radiation the Necrons suffered under, long ago, on their original homeworld, when they were still weak creatures of flesh and bone."/>







</language>
